1
00:00:05,133 --> 00:00:12,133
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:31,800 --> 00:00:32,767
[TIRES SCREECHING]

3
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:35,167
[ENGINE REVVING]

4
00:00:40,100 --> 00:00:41,167
[TIRES SCREECH]

5
00:00:42,467 --> 00:00:44,200
[ENGINES REVVING]

6
00:00:44,200 --> 00:00:45,267
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

7
00:00:45,267 --> 00:00:46,333
[LOUD CRASH]

8
00:00:47,100 --> 00:00:48,233
[TIRES SCREECHING]

9
00:00:50,200 --> 00:00:51,233
<i>- Stop!
- [GUNSHOT]</i>

10
00:00:52,867 --> 00:00:54,133
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

11
00:00:54,133 --> 00:00:55,467
- [ENGINES REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

12
00:00:56,700 --> 00:00:58,267
[GLASS SHATTERING]

13
00:00:58,267 --> 00:01:00,233
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

14
00:01:01,200 --> 00:01:03,167
[ENGINES REVVING]

15
00:01:05,200 --> 00:01:06,233
[TIRES SCREECHING]

16
00:01:07,367 --> 00:01:09,467
[TIRES SCREECHING]

17
00:01:10,233 --> 00:01:11,833
- [GUNSHOT]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:11,833 --> 00:01:13,233
- [TRUCK HORN BLARES]
- [LOUD CRASH]

19
00:01:13,233 --> 00:01:14,600
[TIRES SCREECHING]

20
00:01:20,233 --> 00:01:22,733
<i>The NLEA was able to bring
those to their safe house.</i>

21
00:01:22,733 --> 00:01:24,133
I already have a plan for that.

22
00:01:24,133 --> 00:01:26,233
<i>Our guns are of higher caliber
than theirs.</i>

23
00:01:26,233 --> 00:01:27,733
<i> Why go at them head-on</i>

24
00:01:27,733 --> 00:01:29,233
<i>when we can take them
by surprise?</i>

25
00:01:29,233 --> 00:01:30,233
<i> Bravo!</i>

26
00:01:30,233 --> 00:01:32,533
<i>Weapons can only
take you so far.</i>

27
00:01:32,533 --> 00:01:33,567
<i>You're going to have
to be careful here.</i>

28
00:01:33,567 --> 00:01:35,400
<i>If someone
becomes suspicious of us,</i>

29
00:01:35,400 --> 00:01:36,733
<i> Sam will be in danger.</i>

30
00:01:36,733 --> 00:01:38,333
<i>- What's going on, ma'am?
- I think that's a person.</i>

31
00:01:38,333 --> 00:01:39,667
<i> It's wearing a red jacket.</i>

32
00:01:39,667 --> 00:01:41,233
<i> That's Sam's jacket.</i>

33
00:01:41,267 --> 00:01:43,267
<i> Tomorrow, I'm going out.</i>

34
00:01:43,267 --> 00:01:44,867
<i>I'm just going to look
for a job.</i>

35
00:01:44,867 --> 00:01:46,267
Love, I'd also like to thank you

36
00:01:46,267 --> 00:01:48,267
<i>for being kind
to my whole family,</i>

37
00:01:48,267 --> 00:01:50,267
<i> especially to our neighbors.</i>

38
00:01:50,267 --> 00:01:51,600
[GABO INHALES DEEPLY]

39
00:01:51,600 --> 00:01:53,333
To be honest...

40
00:01:55,367 --> 00:01:57,800
I never thought
you'd come into my life.

41
00:01:58,433 --> 00:02:01,367
["KUNG KAILANGAN MO AKO"
INSTRUMENTAL PLAYING]

42
00:02:01,367 --> 00:02:02,500
I hope...

43
00:02:05,367 --> 00:02:07,333
I hope this isn't just a dream.

44
00:02:10,367 --> 00:02:12,833
I'm hoping that whatever it is
I'm feeling right now...

45
00:02:14,400 --> 00:02:16,433
stays forever.

46
00:02:16,433 --> 00:02:18,933
["KUNG KAILANGAN MO AKO"
INSTRUMENTAL CONTINUES]

47
00:02:18,933 --> 00:02:21,367
Gloria, I want you
to know that...

48
00:02:22,400 --> 00:02:23,733
I love you so much.

49
00:02:26,400 --> 00:02:28,767
I am grateful to God for that.

50
00:02:33,400 --> 00:02:35,900
["KUNG KAILANGAN MO AKO"
INSTRUMENTAL CONTINUES]

51
00:02:35,900 --> 00:02:36,933
Gloria...

52
00:02:40,400 --> 00:02:41,767
I love you.

53
00:02:50,433 --> 00:02:57,400
["KUNG KAILANGAN MO AKO"
INSTRUMENTAL CONTINUES]

54
00:03:10,467 --> 00:03:13,000
[QUIRKY MUSIC PLAYING]

55
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:16,433
[BOTH CHUCKLING AWKWARDLY]

56
00:03:16,433 --> 00:03:18,100
[GABO] So dusty here.

57
00:03:18,100 --> 00:03:19,933
The bed's full of dust.

58
00:03:19,933 --> 00:03:21,000
[LAUGHS]

59
00:03:21,033 --> 00:03:22,500
Looks like I missed this spot.

60
00:03:23,467 --> 00:03:25,100
Shall we do the laundry now?

61
00:03:25,100 --> 00:03:26,867
- Laundry? [CHUCKLES]
- Mm-hmm.

62
00:03:26,867 --> 00:03:28,000
[QUIRKY MUSIC CONTINUES]

63
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:29,433
[GABO] Uh...

64
00:03:29,433 --> 00:03:30,767
S-Sure thing.

65
00:03:30,767 --> 00:03:32,800
My body's aching again.

66
00:03:32,800 --> 00:03:34,633
[EXHALES SHARPLY]

67
00:03:34,633 --> 00:03:37,033
[SIGHS, GRUNTS]

68
00:03:37,033 --> 00:03:38,000
Let me.

69
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:39,800
I'll carry it.

70
00:03:39,800 --> 00:03:41,800
- No, I've got it.
- I insist.

71
00:03:41,800 --> 00:03:44,500
I'll do it.
I don't want you to get tired.

72
00:03:45,133 --> 00:03:46,467
[QUIRKY MUSIC CONTINUES]

73
00:03:46,467 --> 00:03:49,300
Anyway. Love, is it okay...

74
00:03:49,767 --> 00:03:53,033
if we throw in Papa's clothes
and everyone else's too?

75
00:03:53,033 --> 00:03:54,800
Of course.
Leave everything to me.

76
00:03:54,833 --> 00:03:56,000
Okay then.

77
00:03:57,467 --> 00:03:58,467
[GABO WHISPERS] Almost!

78
00:03:58,900 --> 00:04:00,467
We were so close!

79
00:04:04,500 --> 00:04:05,533
[MUSIC ENDS]

80
00:04:06,500 --> 00:04:07,700
- Dude.
- Yeah?

81
00:04:07,700 --> 00:04:10,500
Let's just check in
with the family...

82
00:04:10,500 --> 00:04:11,500
- Who?
- of the gunshot victim.

83
00:04:11,500 --> 00:04:12,700
Remember them?

84
00:04:12,700 --> 00:04:13,900
I don't think so.

85
00:04:13,900 --> 00:04:16,800
That's already old news.

86
00:04:16,800 --> 00:04:18,800
Wait, what's going on here?

87
00:04:18,800 --> 00:04:20,500
- Look, rescuers are here.
- Hey, kid.

88
00:04:21,500 --> 00:04:22,667
What's happening?

89
00:04:22,667 --> 00:04:24,967
We're looking for the body
of an NCIA agent.

90
00:04:24,967 --> 00:04:26,000
No luck so far.

91
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:27,633
Maybe it got washed
away already.

92
00:04:27,667 --> 00:04:29,567
NCIA...

93
00:04:29,567 --> 00:04:30,600
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

94
00:04:30,600 --> 00:04:31,700
What's their name?

95
00:04:31,700 --> 00:04:32,800
[RESCUER] Jacinto.

96
00:04:33,533 --> 00:04:35,433
Jacin... Hang on, wait.

97
00:04:35,433 --> 00:04:37,067
Samantha Jacinto?

98
00:04:37,067 --> 00:04:39,400
Ricardo's daughter is dead.

99
00:04:40,033 --> 00:04:41,167
Wait, wait, wait.

100
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:43,400
- I'll start rolling.
- Go on, shoot.

101
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:49,000
Over there.

102
00:04:50,533 --> 00:04:57,500
[GLOOMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

103
00:05:03,100 --> 00:05:10,033
[SORROWFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

104
00:05:24,567 --> 00:05:31,533
[SORROWFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

105
00:05:34,767 --> 00:05:36,533
[SEBASTIAN]
Sir, this is Sam's jacket.

106
00:05:37,133 --> 00:05:38,967
It was found in the river,

107
00:05:39,900 --> 00:05:41,200
riddled with bullets.

108
00:05:42,967 --> 00:05:49,067
A Rapid DNA test confirmed
it belonged to her,

109
00:05:49,067 --> 00:05:51,200
based on the blood
on the jacket.

110
00:05:53,233 --> 00:05:55,133
[KAREN] Sir, Sam didn't survive.

111
00:05:55,833 --> 00:05:57,467
There were too many
bullet holes.

112
00:05:58,133 --> 00:06:00,467
They made sure she was dead.

113
00:06:00,467 --> 00:06:05,733
[SORROWFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

114
00:06:05,733 --> 00:06:07,100
Would you like to...

115
00:06:07,100 --> 00:06:09,233
inform General Jacinto?

116
00:06:12,200 --> 00:06:13,767
You may go.

117
00:06:20,100 --> 00:06:27,067
[SORROWFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

118
00:06:48,533 --> 00:06:49,633
[FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]

119
00:06:49,633 --> 00:06:50,667
[PIA] Guys.

120
00:06:53,167 --> 00:06:54,200
Good news.

121
00:06:54,833 --> 00:06:58,100
Team Alpha lost an agent.

122
00:06:58,333 --> 00:07:05,300
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

123
00:07:17,200 --> 00:07:18,233
[STAMMERS]

124
00:07:18,233 --> 00:07:19,633
I mean Rallos.

125
00:07:21,033 --> 00:07:24,700
He was tasked
with leading the training

126
00:07:24,700 --> 00:07:27,200
of new teams
that would replace...

127
00:07:27,200 --> 00:07:30,233
Team Charlie and Team Bravo.

128
00:07:30,233 --> 00:07:32,200
He's not dead yet.

129
00:07:32,200 --> 00:07:34,700
What's with the long faces?

130
00:07:34,700 --> 00:07:37,167
Because there's bad news.

131
00:07:37,167 --> 00:07:41,167
[GLOOMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

132
00:07:41,167 --> 00:07:42,133
What is it?

133
00:07:43,233 --> 00:07:44,533
[SIGHS HEAVILY]

134
00:07:47,933 --> 00:07:49,000
[EXHALES]

135
00:07:50,267 --> 00:07:52,200
Sam's jacket was found...

136
00:07:54,033 --> 00:07:55,200
in the river.

137
00:07:55,733 --> 00:07:57,867
It was riddled with bullets.

138
00:07:59,067 --> 00:08:00,033
But...

139
00:08:00,933 --> 00:08:02,733
they didn't find her body.

140
00:08:02,733 --> 00:08:05,900
[GLOOMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

141
00:08:06,133 --> 00:08:07,200
[SNIFFLES]

142
00:08:10,800 --> 00:08:12,200
That really is bad news.

143
00:08:16,233 --> 00:08:22,033
[GLOOMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

144
00:08:22,933 --> 00:08:24,100
[PIA CLEARS THROAT]

145
00:08:24,300 --> 00:08:26,933
I'm sorry for your loss,
Team Alpha.

146
00:08:29,667 --> 00:08:32,267
But there's nothing we can do

147
00:08:32,267 --> 00:08:34,600
but accept it
and move on.

148
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:37,067
Move on?

149
00:08:38,300 --> 00:08:40,267
- Ma'am Pia, move on?!
- Karen!

150
00:08:40,967 --> 00:08:43,167
Is it really that easy
for you to say?

151
00:08:43,167 --> 00:08:45,167
What do you think?
That we'll just accept this?

152
00:08:45,167 --> 00:08:48,900
Wait, please don't take
what I'm saying the wrong way.

153
00:08:48,900 --> 00:08:52,367
All I want is for you guys
not to lose hope.

154
00:08:52,833 --> 00:08:54,067
You're agents.

155
00:08:54,800 --> 00:08:56,300
The country needs you.

156
00:08:56,300 --> 00:08:59,367
[GLOOMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

157
00:08:59,367 --> 00:09:00,800
You know, guys,

158
00:09:02,833 --> 00:09:04,167
I think Ma'am Pia's right.

159
00:09:05,133 --> 00:09:10,333
Sometimes, solving a case
doesn't mean saving a life.

160
00:09:10,867 --> 00:09:17,767
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

161
00:09:26,300 --> 00:09:27,733
[SIGHS]

162
00:09:36,833 --> 00:09:38,867
I'll do the laundry.
I can handle it.

163
00:09:39,400 --> 00:09:41,233
Gabo, what are you doing?
I'll do it.

164
00:09:41,233 --> 00:09:43,233
Come on, you haven't
fully recovered.

165
00:09:43,233 --> 00:09:45,000
Let me do the laundry for now.

166
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:47,033
I'll do it, honey.
I'll wash these.

167
00:09:47,033 --> 00:09:49,200
No, I'll do it. Come on.

168
00:09:49,300 --> 00:09:50,333
I'll do it.

169
00:09:51,967 --> 00:09:53,033
Are you sure?

170
00:09:53,033 --> 00:09:54,767
Yeah, I can handle it.

171
00:09:56,500 --> 00:09:57,800
I'll go ahead.

172
00:09:59,467 --> 00:10:00,833
Honey, I'll do it!

173
00:10:01,733 --> 00:10:03,900
[DIDAY] Hey, Gloria,
where are you going?

174
00:10:03,900 --> 00:10:05,733
Oh, I'm going to
do the laundry.

175
00:10:05,733 --> 00:10:07,233
Do you even know how
to do laundry?

176
00:10:07,233 --> 00:10:08,700
With skin that smooth?

177
00:10:09,067 --> 00:10:10,167
I think so.

178
00:10:11,733 --> 00:10:13,933
Estong, get our dirty clothes.

179
00:10:13,933 --> 00:10:16,033
We'll do the laundry
with Gloria.

180
00:10:16,033 --> 00:10:17,367
- Are you serious, Ma?
- Yes!

181
00:10:17,367 --> 00:10:18,867
We really have a lot of laundry.

182
00:10:18,867 --> 00:10:20,867
Go get them!
Kulas, help your son.

183
00:10:20,867 --> 00:10:22,733
Hurry up. We'll do the
laundry with Gloria.

184
00:10:22,733 --> 00:10:24,100
Come on, Pa.
Let's get the clothes.

185
00:10:24,100 --> 00:10:25,533
- Come on, Gloria.
- Oh.

186
00:10:25,533 --> 00:10:27,067
Here, sit over there.

187
00:10:27,067 --> 00:10:29,300
Here's a little stool.
And here's a basin.

188
00:10:32,400 --> 00:10:33,633
Thank you.

189
00:10:34,733 --> 00:10:36,600
- [ESTONG GRUNTS]
- That's a lot!

190
00:10:36,600 --> 00:10:39,733
I told you earlier, we've got
a lot of laundry piled up!

191
00:10:39,733 --> 00:10:41,367
Okay, okay. It's fine.

192
00:10:41,767 --> 00:10:43,567
Gabo's so lucky.

193
00:10:43,567 --> 00:10:45,267
Not only is Gloria beautiful,

194
00:10:45,267 --> 00:10:46,633
she knows how to take care
of a home, too.

195
00:10:46,633 --> 00:10:48,767
Well, Gabo really knows
how to pick 'em.

196
00:10:48,767 --> 00:10:50,433
Do you have any soap?

197
00:10:50,433 --> 00:10:52,600
- No, I don't.
- [ESTONG] Here, Gloria.

198
00:10:52,600 --> 00:10:53,733
[GLORIA] Thank you.

199
00:10:53,733 --> 00:10:55,400
[DIDAY] Go ahead and
fill it with water.

200
00:10:55,600 --> 00:11:02,400
["TUNAY NA LIGAYA"
BY JUAN KARLOS PLAYING]

201
00:11:16,667 --> 00:11:23,600
["TUNAY NA LIGAYA" CONTINUES]

202
00:11:25,767 --> 00:11:31,400
[TIRES SCREECHING]

203
00:11:31,400 --> 00:11:32,367
[VAN DOOR OPENS]

204
00:11:36,100 --> 00:11:37,600
[VAN DOOR SLIDES OPEN]

205
00:11:41,800 --> 00:11:43,567
Um...

206
00:11:43,633 --> 00:11:48,067
Good afternoon. I'm Dir. Delgado
of the NCIA.

207
00:11:48,667 --> 00:11:51,033
I would like to talk
to General Jacinto.

208
00:11:51,033 --> 00:11:53,733
- Are you Ma'am Sam's boss?
- I am.

209
00:11:54,700 --> 00:11:59,100
- Is her father inside?
- Come on in. Come.

210
00:11:59,100 --> 00:12:02,500
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

211
00:12:02,500 --> 00:12:03,500
[KNOCKS ON DOOR]

212
00:12:04,633 --> 00:12:05,600
Sir.

213
00:12:06,800 --> 00:12:08,600
Ma'am Sam's boss is here.

214
00:12:09,633 --> 00:12:10,667
Let him in.

215
00:12:15,533 --> 00:12:16,533
Dir. Delgado?

216
00:12:18,800 --> 00:12:22,333
I came here because
I have important news.

217
00:12:23,833 --> 00:12:25,967
- Leave us.
- Yes, sir.

218
00:12:26,733 --> 00:12:27,667
Let's go.

219
00:12:29,500 --> 00:12:30,467
Please.

220
00:12:30,900 --> 00:12:31,933
- [DELGADO GROANS]
- [DOOR SHUTS]

221
00:12:32,733 --> 00:12:39,700
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

222
00:12:42,133 --> 00:12:46,533
The NCIA searching for Sam
is a personal matter to me.

223
00:12:47,700 --> 00:12:50,700
You know I also see her
as my daughter.

224
00:12:51,500 --> 00:12:53,633
Why are you here?
Do you have bad news?

225
00:12:54,867 --> 00:12:58,500
My agents found...

226
00:13:00,067 --> 00:13:03,000
the jacket
Sam was wearing the night...

227
00:13:03,900 --> 00:13:05,033
...she disappeared.

228
00:13:06,900 --> 00:13:07,900
[BAG ZIPS OPEN]

229
00:13:08,700 --> 00:13:12,433
[ZIPLOCK BAG RUSTLING]

230
00:13:12,433 --> 00:13:17,433
[MUSIC TURNS DRAMATIC]

231
00:13:17,433 --> 00:13:18,700
It's riddled with bullets.

232
00:13:23,067 --> 00:13:26,033
We only found her jacket,
not her body.

233
00:13:26,900 --> 00:13:29,900
- [ZIPLOCK BAG RUSTLING]
- [JACKET RUSTLES]

234
00:13:32,033 --> 00:13:39,000
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

235
00:13:40,567 --> 00:13:42,533
No one could've survived this.

236
00:13:43,200 --> 00:13:44,400
I'm sorry.

237
00:13:45,733 --> 00:13:49,933
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

238
00:13:49,933 --> 00:13:50,900
W-Why?

239
00:13:54,100 --> 00:13:55,500
What are you trying to say?

240
00:13:57,567 --> 00:13:58,967
My daughter is not dead!

241
00:13:58,967 --> 00:14:05,900
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

242
00:14:06,967 --> 00:14:08,033
Where did you find this?

243
00:14:09,900 --> 00:14:11,533
In Ginintuang Lupa.

244
00:14:12,267 --> 00:14:18,133
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

245
00:14:18,133 --> 00:14:19,533
Ginintuang Lupa.

246
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:23,433
Sorry, Ricardo.

247
00:14:25,767 --> 00:14:32,733
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

248
00:14:46,167 --> 00:14:47,233
[DIDAY] Gloria!

249
00:14:48,133 --> 00:14:50,200
That's not how you wash clothes!

250
00:14:50,200 --> 00:14:53,600
You're rubbing your hands.
You'll get scars from that!

251
00:14:53,600 --> 00:14:56,767
You rub the shirt itself!
It's like this, see?

252
00:14:57,500 --> 00:15:00,167
Ah. I'm sorry,
I just forgot.

253
00:15:00,167 --> 00:15:01,867
Do you really know
how to do this?

254
00:15:01,900 --> 00:15:03,567
I just forgot.

255
00:15:03,567 --> 00:15:06,567
[KULAS]
Gloria, look at Diday's hands.

256
00:15:06,567 --> 00:15:07,833
They're like sweet potatoes.

257
00:15:07,833 --> 00:15:11,033
So take care of your hands
so it doesn't get scars.

258
00:15:11,033 --> 00:15:12,800
[DIDAY] You're such a jerk!

259
00:15:12,800 --> 00:15:15,833
You know, your dead skin sticks
on your clothes

260
00:15:15,833 --> 00:15:17,200
'cause you're too lazy
to shower!

261
00:15:18,067 --> 00:15:19,567
[GLORIA CHUCKLES]

262
00:15:19,567 --> 00:15:20,600
Love.

263
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:23,133
- Gabo.
- I'll do that.

264
00:15:23,133 --> 00:15:26,333
- Your hands might get hurt.
- No, it's okay!

265
00:15:26,333 --> 00:15:28,667
Estong, grab me the bench.

266
00:15:28,667 --> 00:15:30,567
- Sure, Gabo.
- I'll help my wife.

267
00:15:30,567 --> 00:15:32,200
- Can you manage?
- [GABO] Yes.

268
00:15:32,200 --> 00:15:33,167
Here, Gabo.

269
00:15:33,967 --> 00:15:36,067
[BENCH THUDS, SCRAPES]

270
00:15:36,100 --> 00:15:38,033
- [GABO GROANS]
- Here, I'll teach you.

271
00:15:38,033 --> 00:15:39,833
- [KULAS] Add some water here.
- [GABO GROANS]

272
00:15:41,600 --> 00:15:43,200
I'll teach you
how to wash clothes.

273
00:15:43,200 --> 00:15:45,567
[GABO GROANING]

274
00:15:46,933 --> 00:15:49,000
You have to soak it first.

275
00:15:50,700 --> 00:15:53,000
When you soak it,
it'll get some soap too.

276
00:15:54,333 --> 00:15:57,700
Then you rub it with more soap.

277
00:15:57,700 --> 00:16:01,867
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

278
00:16:01,867 --> 00:16:03,000
Copy what I'm doing.

279
00:16:04,767 --> 00:16:06,333
Rub the other parts
with soap.

280
00:16:07,800 --> 00:16:10,067
This is how you rub it properly.

281
00:16:10,067 --> 00:16:13,033
Hold it tight,
then rub it like this.

282
00:16:13,033 --> 00:16:15,233
Hey! Neighbors!

283
00:16:15,233 --> 00:16:19,233
If you have tons of laundry,
go and wash it with us!

284
00:16:19,233 --> 00:16:21,200
Let's join them, come on!

285
00:16:21,200 --> 00:16:27,800
[OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

286
00:16:27,800 --> 00:16:30,600
- [DIDAY] See?
- This will be fun.

287
00:16:31,767 --> 00:16:33,000
[GABO CHUCKLES]

288
00:16:38,767 --> 00:16:40,100
[PHONE RINGING]

289
00:16:42,233 --> 00:16:44,233
- Yes, General?
- [RICARDO]  Domingo.

290
00:16:44,933 --> 00:16:45,933
Delgado is at my house,

291
00:16:45,933 --> 00:16:48,100
and he's saying
that Sam may be gone.

292
00:16:48,100 --> 00:16:49,733
That my daughter is dead!

293
00:16:49,733 --> 00:16:53,100
W-What? We don't know
about that, Gen. Jacinto.

294
00:16:53,100 --> 00:16:54,867
That's the problem!

295
00:16:54,933 --> 00:16:57,233
They found Sam's jacket
that was riddled with bullets!

296
00:16:58,000 --> 00:16:59,267
<i> Do you not coordinate?!</i>

297
00:16:59,267 --> 00:17:01,233
Or are you trying to one-up
each other?

298
00:17:02,067 --> 00:17:03,800
Well, you listen to me.

299
00:17:03,800 --> 00:17:06,133
You better start cooperating
because I will not accept

300
00:17:06,133 --> 00:17:07,933
that my daughter is dead!

301
00:17:07,933 --> 00:17:09,833
- Yes, Gen--
- [LINE DROPS]

302
00:17:09,833 --> 00:17:10,800
[PHONE THUDS]

303
00:17:11,933 --> 00:17:14,267
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

304
00:17:14,267 --> 00:17:16,267
The NCIA abandoned my daughter.

305
00:17:16,300 --> 00:17:18,000
That's not true, Ricardo.

306
00:17:18,867 --> 00:17:21,000
While she was working,
while we were searching for her,

307
00:17:21,000 --> 00:17:23,133
we did not abandon Sam.

308
00:17:23,133 --> 00:17:25,033
No. You knew!

309
00:17:25,033 --> 00:17:27,433
You knew how dangerous
the Zafra case was!

310
00:17:28,700 --> 00:17:30,200
And yet you still let her
handle it!

311
00:17:30,200 --> 00:17:32,667
It was all because
of Sam's skills and abilities!

312
00:17:32,667 --> 00:17:34,033
And now she's gone!

313
00:17:34,033 --> 00:17:35,900
No one wanted this, Ricardo.

314
00:17:36,700 --> 00:17:40,667
I'm the one who stood
as Sam's father in the NCIA,

315
00:17:40,667 --> 00:17:44,000
so this has been hurting me
so much.

316
00:17:47,267 --> 00:17:51,000
I don't want to see your face
nor any of your agents

317
00:17:51,033 --> 00:17:52,300
here in my house!

318
00:17:53,200 --> 00:17:55,167
You will not be paying respects
to my daughter.

319
00:17:55,167 --> 00:18:00,800
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

320
00:18:00,800 --> 00:18:02,300
[RICARDO] You and your NCIA!

321
00:18:03,167 --> 00:18:05,800
You're the ones to blame
for Sam's disappearance!

322
00:18:10,133 --> 00:18:11,100
Get out.

323
00:18:13,133 --> 00:18:14,100
Get out!

324
00:18:14,900 --> 00:18:16,200
[ZIPLOCK BAG RUSTLES]

325
00:18:16,200 --> 00:18:18,333
[RETREATING FOOTSTEPS]

326
00:18:18,333 --> 00:18:19,700
[DOOR OPENS, CLOSES]

327
00:18:22,267 --> 00:18:23,200
[ISOBEL] Ah.

328
00:18:24,867 --> 00:18:26,133
Dir. Delgado?

329
00:18:27,500 --> 00:18:28,967
Isobel.

330
00:18:33,367 --> 00:18:35,033
This jacket belongs to Sam.

331
00:18:35,033 --> 00:18:36,833
Have you found her?

332
00:18:40,367 --> 00:18:42,000
What happened to it?

333
00:18:42,333 --> 00:18:44,367
Why is it full of holes?

334
00:18:44,367 --> 00:18:46,033
What happened to my daughter?

335
00:18:46,033 --> 00:18:49,000
Sam was gunned down
by some wicked men.

336
00:18:51,267 --> 00:18:52,867
I'm so sorry.

337
00:18:53,400 --> 00:18:57,067
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

338
00:19:00,133 --> 00:19:01,533
[VOICE BREAKS] Ricardo...

339
00:19:03,400 --> 00:19:04,433
Explain this.

340
00:19:04,433 --> 00:19:05,933
They say Sam's dead.

341
00:19:06,267 --> 00:19:08,067
My daughter is dead?

342
00:19:10,233 --> 00:19:12,200
My daughter is dead...

343
00:19:14,900 --> 00:19:17,933
[ISOBEL SOBBING]

344
00:19:17,933 --> 00:19:19,900
[TWINKLE] Ma'am...

345
00:19:19,900 --> 00:19:23,067
The fortune teller was
right all along!

346
00:19:23,067 --> 00:19:25,900
[SOBBING]

347
00:19:25,900 --> 00:19:27,233
- My daughter is dead!
- Ma'am...

348
00:19:27,233 --> 00:19:29,567
She's gone!
She's gone forever!

349
00:19:29,600 --> 00:19:31,467
- Sir...
- She's dead!

350
00:19:31,467 --> 00:19:35,100
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC PLAYING]

351
00:19:35,100 --> 00:19:36,767
Sam...

352
00:19:37,100 --> 00:19:39,300
Sam...

353
00:19:44,167 --> 00:19:47,133
My daughter Sam...

354
00:19:49,100 --> 00:19:52,867
[ISOBEL SOBBING]

355
00:19:54,233 --> 00:19:55,300
[GUN CLICKS]

356
00:19:56,067 --> 00:20:02,967
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

357
00:20:03,433 --> 00:20:04,667
Boss Django.

358
00:20:05,300 --> 00:20:06,967
You're really something.

359
00:20:06,967 --> 00:20:08,500
Boss Mariano actually
believed you.

360
00:20:09,167 --> 00:20:12,033
But why does it seem like
you're just following...

361
00:20:12,033 --> 00:20:13,100
Lucas, was it?

362
00:20:15,967 --> 00:20:17,067
You idiots!

363
00:20:19,100 --> 00:20:21,067
When have I ever
followed anyone?

364
00:20:22,100 --> 00:20:25,067
I'm just letting them believe
I'm taking orders from them.

365
00:20:25,533 --> 00:20:27,533
Until Mariano sees

366
00:20:27,533 --> 00:20:30,233
who's really better,
me or his son.

367
00:20:32,100 --> 00:20:33,333
[CHUCKLES MENACINGLY]

368
00:20:41,333 --> 00:20:43,033
You're being summoned!

369
00:20:46,167 --> 00:20:53,100
[OMINOUS MUSIC CONTINUES]

370
00:21:03,133 --> 00:21:06,233
Ma, I thought Dad
trusted me now.

371
00:21:06,233 --> 00:21:08,967
But why does he still trust
outsiders?

372
00:21:09,000 --> 00:21:11,333
Just trust your father's
instincts.

373
00:21:11,333 --> 00:21:13,567
Just because he listens
to Django

374
00:21:13,567 --> 00:21:15,733
doesn't mean he doesn't
trust you.

375
00:21:18,233 --> 00:21:20,233
A person gets sharper

376
00:21:20,233 --> 00:21:22,467
when they have someone
to compete with.

377
00:21:23,267 --> 00:21:25,167
So show your father

378
00:21:25,167 --> 00:21:28,167
that no matter who he puts
against you,

379
00:21:28,167 --> 00:21:30,133
you can take them down.

380
00:21:32,400 --> 00:21:33,667
Yes, Ma.

381
00:21:33,667 --> 00:21:37,567
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

382
00:21:41,400 --> 00:21:43,367
Boss, everything's ready.

383
00:21:44,533 --> 00:21:46,700
You already know your mission.

384
00:21:46,700 --> 00:21:49,733
Get the gold, but remember,

385
00:21:49,733 --> 00:21:54,067
your lives mean nothing to me
if anything happens to my son.

386
00:21:54,533 --> 00:21:56,167
- Yes, ma'am.
- Yes, ma'am.

387
00:21:57,233 --> 00:21:58,433
[LUCAS] Let's go.

388
00:22:00,800 --> 00:22:07,667
[MUSIC BECOMES OMINOUS]

389
00:22:18,100 --> 00:22:19,467
Listen up, everyone!

390
00:22:20,667 --> 00:22:23,633
We're not letting the NLEA
take what's ours.

391
00:22:24,467 --> 00:22:26,067
You already know what to do.

392
00:22:26,067 --> 00:22:28,467
If anyone gets in your way,
take them out.

393
00:22:29,333 --> 00:22:30,567
You're in charge.

394
00:22:31,100 --> 00:22:32,300
You're the boss.

395
00:22:32,800 --> 00:22:34,133
Let's go!

396
00:22:37,167 --> 00:22:38,767
Wait.

397
00:22:38,833 --> 00:22:42,267
Don't forget that I'm the one
calling the shots here.

398
00:22:42,833 --> 00:22:44,167
Yes, boss!

399
00:22:44,167 --> 00:22:46,633
I'll do whatever you order.

400
00:22:47,167 --> 00:22:49,133
[CHUCKLING]

401
00:22:50,167 --> 00:22:52,133
The moment you disobey me,

402
00:22:53,700 --> 00:22:55,633
I'll take you out myself.

403
00:22:55,633 --> 00:22:56,667
Understood, Boss.

404
00:22:57,300 --> 00:22:58,833
You're the king here.

405
00:22:59,100 --> 00:23:00,667
We'll do whatever you say,

406
00:23:01,367 --> 00:23:02,633
no questions asked.

407
00:23:02,867 --> 00:23:05,800
[CHUCKLING]

408
00:23:06,867 --> 00:23:10,733
[ENGINES STARTING]

409
00:23:12,667 --> 00:23:13,800
Let's go!

410
00:23:13,800 --> 00:23:16,800
[OMINOUS MUSIC CONTINUES]

411
00:23:16,800 --> 00:23:20,667
[TIRES SCREECHING]

412
00:23:20,667 --> 00:23:22,567
[MUSIC FADES]

413
00:23:24,167 --> 00:23:25,733
Miss Diday, she's learning.

414
00:23:25,733 --> 00:23:28,333
Gabo, she looks like
she's from a rich family.

415
00:23:28,333 --> 00:23:30,133
She doesn't know
how to do laundry.

416
00:23:30,133 --> 00:23:31,333
[GIGGLES AWKWARDLY]

417
00:23:31,900 --> 00:23:33,500
Can I ask you something?

418
00:23:33,500 --> 00:23:35,400
- How long have you...
- What is it?

419
00:23:35,400 --> 00:23:37,900
- You're such a gossip!
- [BOTH GIGGLING]

420
00:23:37,900 --> 00:23:40,567
How long have you and
Sir Kulas been together?

421
00:23:40,567 --> 00:23:42,900
- Living together?
- Yes.

422
00:23:42,900 --> 00:23:44,833
You know, I was forced into it.

423
00:23:44,833 --> 00:23:47,233
We've been together
for 33 years.

424
00:23:47,233 --> 00:23:49,233
- So, Sir...
- Sir Kulas.

425
00:23:49,233 --> 00:23:50,633
Sir Kulas?

426
00:23:50,633 --> 00:23:54,400
How many wives has
Miss Diday been for you?

427
00:23:54,400 --> 00:23:56,133
[DIDAY] I'll answer that.

428
00:23:56,867 --> 00:23:58,533
I'm his fifth wife.

429
00:23:58,767 --> 00:24:00,600
- Fifth?
- It's true!

430
00:24:00,600 --> 00:24:03,900
But his naughtiness wouldn't
work with me because...

431
00:24:03,900 --> 00:24:06,600
he had to marry me,
or I'd kill him.

432
00:24:06,600 --> 00:24:07,867
[LAUGHTER]

433
00:24:07,867 --> 00:24:09,367
Sir Kulas!

434
00:24:09,367 --> 00:24:14,433
In your life now, is Miss Diday
the only woman you love?

435
00:24:14,433 --> 00:24:16,600
- Of course.
- [DIDAY] Answer properly.

436
00:24:16,600 --> 00:24:17,667
I said, of course!

437
00:24:17,667 --> 00:24:18,933
Why am I being forced?

438
00:24:18,933 --> 00:24:20,933
[LAUGHTER]

439
00:24:20,933 --> 00:24:23,933
You're my last one!
Forever.

440
00:24:23,933 --> 00:24:26,367
- [DIDAY] Wow.
- You're the only one, Diday.

441
00:24:27,567 --> 00:24:29,167
That's why, honey...

442
00:24:30,533 --> 00:24:31,933
I promise you...

443
00:24:33,767 --> 00:24:36,900
you're the only woman I'll love
for the rest of my life.

444
00:24:45,267 --> 00:24:46,667
[BOTH GIGGLING]

445
00:24:46,933 --> 00:24:52,233
["TUNAY NA LIGAYA"
INSTRUMENTAL PLAYING]

446
00:24:52,233 --> 00:24:54,533
See? When you put
your mind to it,

447
00:24:54,533 --> 00:24:55,700
it's easy.

448
00:24:57,567 --> 00:24:58,667
Just like that.

449
00:24:59,800 --> 00:25:01,467
You know, when I was a kid,

450
00:25:01,500 --> 00:25:02,833
I loved doing the laundry

451
00:25:02,833 --> 00:25:04,967
because I used to play
with the bubbles.

452
00:25:07,733 --> 00:25:09,200
Like this.

453
00:25:09,667 --> 00:25:16,567
["TUNAY NA LIGAYA" CONTINUES]

454
00:25:33,600 --> 00:25:38,100
[GABO BLOWING BUBBLES]

455
00:25:42,967 --> 00:25:45,100
See? You've got bubbles now.

456
00:25:45,100 --> 00:25:48,600
[GABO CHUCKLING]

457
00:25:48,600 --> 00:25:55,600
["TUNAY NA LIGAYA"
BY JUAN KARLOS PLAYING]

458
00:25:58,667 --> 00:26:00,300
You've got bubbles, too!

459
00:26:02,000 --> 00:26:04,200
[BOTH CHUCKLING]

460
00:26:04,200 --> 00:26:09,600
["TUNAY NA LIGAYA" CONTINUES]

461
00:26:09,633 --> 00:26:11,867
Mameng, look at Gabo.

462
00:26:12,700 --> 00:26:14,833
Ever since he was a child...

463
00:26:15,700 --> 00:26:18,000
This is the first time
I've seen him this happy.

464
00:26:21,733 --> 00:26:23,933
[MAMENG] Gloria is very kind.

465
00:26:24,367 --> 00:26:26,967
Her every move is like
a breath of fresh air

466
00:26:26,967 --> 00:26:28,900
here in Ginintuang Lupa.

467
00:26:28,900 --> 00:26:32,967
If his relationship with Gloria
becomes real...

468
00:26:32,967 --> 00:26:34,233
[RUDY CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

469
00:26:34,233 --> 00:26:38,133
I might just become the
happiest father in the world.

470
00:26:38,133 --> 00:26:40,167
They're endearing to watch,
aren't they?

471
00:26:40,167 --> 00:26:41,167
Mm-hmm.

472
00:26:46,833 --> 00:26:49,533
[DANTE] They suit each other.
I hope...

473
00:26:50,200 --> 00:26:52,900
- ...they do end up together.
- I sure hope so.

474
00:26:54,067 --> 00:26:55,167
[MAMENG SIGHS FONDLY]

475
00:26:55,900 --> 00:27:02,867
["TUNAY NA LIGAYA" CONTINUES]

476
00:27:17,933 --> 00:27:24,900
["TUNAY NA LIGAYA" CONTINUES]

477
00:27:39,900 --> 00:27:46,867
["TUNAY NA LIGAYA" CONTINUES]

478
00:27:49,100 --> 00:27:52,833
<i>The bar is old,
and the staff are old!</i>

479
00:27:52,833 --> 00:27:55,067
<i>BeerGin will become
more successful</i>

480
00:27:55,067 --> 00:27:57,300
<i>when you aren't
the hostesses anymore!</i>

481
00:27:57,300 --> 00:27:59,067
<i>- Huh?!
- Stop!</i>

482
00:27:59,067 --> 00:28:00,967
<i>We'll go either way.
We outnumber them.</i>

483
00:28:02,800 --> 00:28:04,567
<i> Once Papa Rudy signs it,</i>

484
00:28:04,567 --> 00:28:06,967
<i>he is agreeing
to have all of you evicted</i>

485
00:28:06,967 --> 00:28:08,800
<i>from Ginintuang Lupa
in exchange for money.</i>

486
00:28:08,800 --> 00:28:10,600
<i>She might be starting
to regain her memories.</i>

487
00:28:10,600 --> 00:28:14,067
<i>Gloria, do you remember
anything about your past?</i>

488
00:28:14,067 --> 00:28:15,367
<i> About yourself?</i>
